<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρῠό-εις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>on the brow</i> or <i>edge of a steep rock,
			beetling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴλιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.411
				</span></i>
			; of the Acrocorinthus, Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.92
			</span></i>.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́; μέτωπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					15.106
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρυάω</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., <i>majestic, solemn</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρυόεσσα ἀοιδή</span>, of
			Aeschylus' poetry, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.39
			</span></i> (Antip. Thess.).</div>
